How to Choose the Right Sanitary Pad for Your Flow

Choosing the right sanitary pad can make a big difference to your comfort during your period. With different lengths, sizes, absorbency levels, and designs available, it can sometimes be difficult to decide which pad is best for your individual needs.

The important thing to remember is that there is no single sanitary pad that is perfect for everyone. Your ideal choice depends on your menstrual flow, body, daily activities, and personal comfort.

Understand Your Flow

The first thing to consider is how heavy your menstrual flow is.

Your flow may be lighter at the beginning or end of your period and heavier during the middle days. Because of this, you may not need the same pad throughout your entire cycle.

A regular or smaller pad may be suitable for lighter-flow days. During heavier days, you may prefer a longer pad with greater absorbency.

Consider Pad Length

Pad length is an important factor when choosing menstrual protection.

Longer pads can provide greater front-to-back coverage and may be useful when you experience heavy flow or leakage. They can also be particularly helpful at night because you may move around while sleeping.

For people who experience back leakage, choosing a pad with a longer or wider back can provide additional coverage.

Look for Wings

Many sanitary pads come with wings that fold around the sides of your underwear.

Wings help hold the pad in position and can reduce movement during walking, working, travelling, or exercising.

However, the pad should still fit comfortably. If it bunches or moves frequently, you may need to try a different size or design.

Think About Comfort

Absorbency is important, but comfort matters too.

Some people prefer soft top layers, while others prioritise a thinner design. If you have experienced irritation with a particular product, consider trying a different material or style.

The right pad should feel secure without causing unnecessary discomfort.

Choose According to Your Activity

Your lifestyle can also influence your choice.

If you are travelling or spending several hours outside your home, you may prefer a product with greater absorbency and longer coverage. For overnight use, a longer night pad may provide additional protection.

