You May Need Different Pads for Different Days

There is no rule that says you need to use one pad type throughout your period.

For example, you may use a regular pad on lighter days, a higher-absorbency pad on heavy-flow days, and an overnight pad while sleeping.

Keeping a few suitable options available can make your period easier to manage.

Change Your Pad Regularly

Even a highly absorbent pad should be changed when necessary. Check your pad regularly and replace it when it becomes wet, heavily saturated, uncomfortable, or close to leaking.

Changing your pad regularly is an important part of menstrual hygiene.

Find What Works for You

Choosing the right sanitary pad is ultimately a personal decision. Pay attention to your flow, comfort, leakage, pad movement, and daily routine.

Once you understand what your body needs, choosing a suitable menstrual product becomes much easier.

The goal is simple: find a sanitary pad that provides enough protection while keeping you comfortable and confident throughout your period.
